# Distinct twelve-byte solution: clear AX once, then copy its zero into BX.
11111010 # instruction | CLI | Keep the final native halt stopped.
10111000 00110100 00010010 # instruction | MOV AX,1234 | Establish a nonzero AX; preserve the locked setup.
10111011 01111000 01010110 # instruction | MOV BX,5678 | Establish a nonzero BX; preserve the locked setup.
00110001 11000000 # instruction | XOR AX,AX | Clear AX with a two-byte encoding.
10001001 11000011 # instruction | MOV BX,AX | Copy zero into BX; this encoding preserves the flags from XOR.
11110100 # instruction | HLT | Stop with AX and BX zero and the initial stack pointer unchanged.
